{
  "_comment": [
    "What each claim rests on -- the dependency graph the foundation log's blast-radius column is queried from.",
    "每条 claim 所依赖的东西——地基台账里\"爆炸半径\"那一列的查询来源。",
    "",
    "Two kinds of edge, and both are generated from the code rather than from memory:",
    "  * a compile edge -- a `foc/` header the module (or its own .cpp) includes directly. A change there",
    "    is a change to what the claim was measured against;",
    "  * a semantic edge -- another module whose value the claim quotes without including it. The gain law",
    "    is the example: `core/pi.hpp`'s claim quotes numbers that `motor/motor_config.hpp` computes, and",
    "    if that formula moves the claim is stale while every test still passes.",
    "A self-edge (`core/commissioning.hpp` -> itself) means nothing else in the tree feeds it.",
    "",
    "Every entry is checked by `claim_gate.py`: a path that does not exist, or an identifier that appears",
    "nowhere in include/ or src/, fails the build. That is the point -- a basis that has rotted is worse",
    "than no basis, because the query below would return a confident and wrong blast radius.",
    "",
    "Why this file and not a fifth column in the README. `evidence` answers 'what checks this claim';",
    "`basis` answers 'what would invalidate it'. The two are different: a claim can have evidence that",
    "passes while resting on a plant model that is wrong, which is exactly the W7-c failure.",
    "",
    "QUERY:  python3 .github/misc/gates.py claims --impact <path or identifier>",
    "It prints every claim whose basis names that thing, with the evidence to re-run. Use it before",
    "changing a shared file, and use its output -- never an estimate -- to fill the blast-radius column",
    "of foundation-log.rst.",
    "",
    "Coverage is now complete: every installed header is mapped. `unmapped` stays in the schema (the gate",
    "still enforces that a row is in one list or the other) but is empty, and must stay empty -- a new",
    "header arrives with either a basis or a stated reason it has none."
  ],
